"b0b5230c0f966d9f9baabdacb68b9b53dafd9daa1d4bd43447b7c3d8f5c1aada\", \"decision\": \"defer\", \"reason\": \"Relevant in part under Relevance because it addresses load carriage, pack securing, and plate versus household weight, but its gear content is a few sentences and the calorie figures are Pandolf model estimates rather than measured or gear-tested results (Credibility, Unsupported claims). The publisher discloses affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units, so the pack and plate remarks need weighing for that relationship, and the item should be deferred until a source tests gear under load.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/the-science-behind-why-longevity-doctors-call-rucking-the\", \"version_id\": \"aeda4b5f225800ed1d00b7511b87d31d85b7f4e73a00264d638caf12aa48d92a\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Out of scope under Relevance: this is a training-science essay on longevity and Zone 2 with no tested gear evidence. Its gear mentions, including the COROS PACE 4 as a budget pick and the GORUCK Rucker 5.0 with a lifetime guarantee, are promotional and unsupported, and the publisher discloses affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units (Commercial incentives). Attia quotes come through secondary reporting and the central claims lack independent gear testing.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/tough-ruck-boston-2026-how-to-train-for-a-26-2-mile-memorial\", \"version_id\": \"2f3525a742065261ffdb1f4f6237c5a5295a0ab940c6ec9cf59f22c61c4162b1\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Out of scope under Relevance: Tough Ruck Boston is a different event from Mammoth, and the article covers race logistics, weight divisions, and training plans rather than evaluating gear. Its gear checklist (GORUCK GR2, Mystery Ranch, Salomon Quest 4) has no tested evidence, and the publisher discloses affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units. Official race-brief details are attributed to a brief not supplied here and are not Mammoth requirements.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/weighted-vests-bone-density-research\", \"version_id\": \"1736e04dd80b2647c3debb8f1d214d167b4397f8ed19248df46a976e629c2cdc\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Out of scope under Relevance and Suitability: the article answers whether vests build bone density for midlife women, not whether a vest is good, required, or effective for Mammoth carrying. Its cited studies (Snow 2000, the 2026 Wang meta-analysis, INVEST) are described with appropriate limits, but the article includes a direct product purchase link for price and availability, and the publisher discloses affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/why-guy-fieri-and-other-celebrities-are-trading-gyms-for-ruc\", \"version_id\": \"bba63ffec4090d321324594104ff7e0d001683eba64eeb4a0e6cc88b97c1abdd\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Out of scope under Relevance and Credibility: the piece analyzes a single magazine interview about a celebrity routine and tests no equipment, and the interview cannot isolate the vest's contribution. Its product references point to the publisher's own buying guides and are not endorsements, and the publisher discloses affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units. No gear performance evidence is presented.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/pillars/rucking-for-weight-loss\", \"version_id\": \"08db949f0cdc7287a207a42c46be83003fa1aa97bb2c2d2ddbbbc8bccba71ed2\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Out of scope under Relevance: this is a weight-loss program built around calorie-deficit nutrition and a bundled starter kit (pack, plate, socks, anti-chafe, water) presented as a purchase path, not an evaluation of gear for Mammoth. Calorie figures are Pandolf model estimates, many claims lack sources, and the publisher discloses affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units, which weigh against it under Commercial incentives and Unsupported claims.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/training/30-lb-vs-45-lb-ruck-when-to-make-the-jump\", \"version_id\": \"badaf2e9d36d7f074dce0baafb9b8f94d1e68eb4b1a1f3f9a8fe4de235c2368b\", \"decision\": \"defer\", \"reason\": \"Relevant in part under Relevance because carried load over hours is central to Mammoth conditions, but the 7 percent calorie difference and the progression intervals are Pandolf model outputs and planning examples, not measured or field-tested results (Credibility, Unsupported claims). The 45 lb plate guidance is GORUCK manufacturer guidance without independent corroboration, and the publisher discloses affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units, so defer until independent field evidence on load tolerance is available.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/training/does-rucking-build-muscle\", \"version_id\": \"f26d136ea2ff7722dbeff53b9e4b2556ee4f1d44a6e17e54a1b61da9a412b091\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Out of scope under Relevance: the article addresses muscle hypertrophy and training physiology rather than whether any gear is good, required, or effective at Mammoth. Its one cited review (Knapik 2012) concerns load-carriage performance rather than equipment, and the gear mentions are minor. The publisher discloses affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units, which the Commercial incentives rule requires us to note.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/training/rucking-vs-crossfit\", \"version_id\": \"2ec50078088d9edb6aa3da2a98bf31fc35436f48bdf1b2a079af60044eed5f81\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Out of scope under Relevance: this compares training modalities (CrossFit and rucking) and presents no tested gear evidence. Its one gear claim, that the GORUCK Rucker 5.0 is made for plate carry and repeated handling, is an unsupported manufacturer-style assertion, and the publisher discloses affiliate commissions and GORUCK-supplied review units. The article itself notes that injury rates across populations are not comparable, so it offers no evidence for a gear conclusion.\", \"piece_ids\": []}","ttft_ms":38039,"type":"result","duration_ms":48411,"uuid":"3170bf42-9f2c-4f03-922a-64d8436fe3db","ttft_stream_ms":920,"time_to_request_ms":145,"first_content_frame_ms":920,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
